  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nAs high pressure continues to linger over the area, Thursday \nwill still see warmer than normal temperatures. Later Thursday, \na shortwave trough ahead of a large Pacific trough off the coast\nof British Columbia will dig across our area. This shortwave \nwill return precipitation chances, mainly over the northernmost \nmountain portions of the CWA. The cold front associated with \nthis trough will bring gusty winds from the west and a cooldown \nto normal or slightly below normal temperatures Friday through \nSaturday. Come late Saturday, the larger parent trough is \nprojected to steer inland and over our area as a closed upper \nlow, continuing a cooling trend and breezy west winds. For now, \nlong- range guidance mainly favors widespread precipitation over\nthe northern half of our CWA Saturday through Sunday. Monday \nwill be dry, breezy, and cool as the upper low steers out east.",
